      "message": "I still think it should be harmless to have a lock to protect this, in case in the future someone changes the behavior of AP or OS that concurrency happens.  \n\nGiven the flag is shared and check fan status is a HW behavior which may take longer time, one race condition is that concurrency happens with both getting OVERRIDE_CHECK, and the first is about to finish so turn off the fan while the latter is about to check fan rpm, then the final result will be OVERRIDE_NONE.  \nYou may also have to include `#include \"task.h\"`.\n```suggestion\nK_MUTEX_DEFINE(check_fan_lock);\nint cbi_board_override(enum cbi_data_tag tag, uint8_t *buf, uint8_t *size)\n{\n        mutex_lock(\u0026 check_fan_lock);\n\tif (override_flag \u003d\u003d OVERRIDE_CHECK)\n\t\tcheck_fan_status();\n        mutex_unlock(\u0026 check_fan_lock);\n```",
